# VIGIL calibration — environment for the process that runs the calibration model gateway.
# Copy to ~/.config/vigil/calibration.env (chmod 600) and fill in.
# =====================================================================
# The provider key is NEVER written in this file. The gateway reads it from an AWS SSM Parameter Store
# SecureString (the owner creates it in the AWS console: Systems Manager > Parameter Store; AWS-DEPLOY.md), with
# the host's instance role (provision.sh grants ssm:GetParameter on this one parameter). With this set, SSM is the
# gateway's ONLY key source: a key in the environment or in sigil.env is ignored, and a missing region, a missing
# aws CLI, a parameter that is not a SecureString or one the role cannot read stops the gateway from starting.
# The key is read when the gateway starts: after changing it in SSM, restart the process.

# owner-set: the SSM SecureString holding the provider key
VIGIL_ANTHROPIC_KEY_SSM_PARAMETER=/vigil/anthropic-api-key
# The AWS region of that parameter (provision.sh prints it), e.g. eu-west-1:
# VIGIL_AWS_REGION=
